&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is composed of several teams that work together to help define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of the Stripe brand and product. Product Design Managers work directly with Engineering leaders, Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Marketers in each product area. Together, they identify the strategy and vision, and drive execution for critical initiatives that create a world-class support experience for all Stripe customers and users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Payments builds on core Stripe financial products and creates solutions that empower businesses to expand into new markets worldwide without the friction of complex global operations. The sheer volume of payments that flow through Stripe on an hourly basis necessitates the highest level of craft and reliability, which means that Global Payments product designers have the chance to create and ship the best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of the Global Payments Design team, you will shape the products and experiences that make it as easy for businesses to sell globally as it is to sell locally. This team oversees product experiences around cross-border commerce, covering local payment methods, global tax compliance, localized consumer experiences, and moving money across borders. You&#39;ll ensure that any business can use Stripe to reach customers anywhere in the world, including fast-growing companies that expect to operate globally from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead and grow a team of experienced designers who have a track record of navigating ambiguity and delivering high-impact solutions that improve payments experiences for Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a growing, business-critical team of designers distributed across EMEA and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand the team to meet business demands and employee development needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Management leaders to identify, shape, and prioritize current and new product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Stripe teams and establish collaboration practices that result in holistic solutions for a horizontal product space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product Management, Product Engineering, Marketing, and senior leadership to drive fast decision making, create clarity, and raise the bar for craft and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and lead designers across experience levels to do the best work of their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 8+ years of relevant design experience at a tech or product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel at motivating and inspiring people to do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience recruiting and building product design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are relentlessly user-focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience designing for complex platforms and enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel at both written and spoken communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You do your best work collaboratively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You find a meaningful balance between speed, quality, and risky but interesting work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

AT COVERON, WE’RE BUILDING A COMPLETE IDENTITY THEFT PROTECTION SERVICE.

Join the team behind Nord Security’s latest product—combining dark web monitoring, credit tracking, and identity theft insurance into one powerful platform.


YOUR IMPACT? HELPING PEOPLE PROTECT THEIR IDENTITIES, SPOT THREATS EARLY, AND RECOVER STRONGER.

MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES

 - Own the mobile app product (iOS & Android) and its development roadmap;

 - Initiate new features that drive business value and unlock new acquisition tactics;

 - Align objectives, expectations, and timeframes across developers, designers, and stakeholders;

 - Manage and prioritize the backlog;

 - Drive team priorities tied to organizational goals;

 - Own business decisions and set feature direction;

 - Monitor product performance and customer behaviour to find growth opportunities;

 - Ensure user privacy and data protection across the product;

 - Define mobile app product requirements, write clear user stories and acceptance criteria for the development team;



CORE REQUIREMENTS

 - 3+ years experience as a Product Owner on mobile app products (iOS & Android);

 - Knowledge of Google Play / App Store requirements and review processes;

 - Understanding of mobile payment ecosystems (in-app purchases, subscriptions, store billing);

 - Experience in a startup or fast-paced environment;

 - Ability to navigate ambiguity independently;

 - Proactivity in raising challenges and identifying solutions;

 - Business-driven mindset: connecting features to growth and monetization;

 - Familiarity with Agile/Scrum and backlog tools (e.g. Jira);

 - Subscription-based B2C product experience is a plus;

 - Digital marketing knowledge is a plus.



WHAT WE OFFER

Innovate with industry leaders

Work alongside global experts to build world-leading cybersecurity tools, impacting millions of users around the world.

Learn & grow

Boost your skills via our extensive training programs (online and offline) & other resources. Benefit from mentorship and career-switch opportunities to grow within the company.

Work in a next-gen Cyber City office

Thrive in our bustling office, featuring ergonomic workspaces, modern meeting rooms, engaging events, and specialty coffee to fuel your day.

Work from anywhere

Recharge with a change of scenery – choose work from any location when you feel a need to power your creativity and drive.

Physical well-being

Boost your health with free-of-charge 24/7 gym access, onsite and online workouts, and consultations led by in-house Physical Well-Being experts.

Mental & emotional health

Nurture your mind with free psychologist consultations, dedicated mental health events, and premium access to top-rated wellness apps like Calm, Headspace, and Mindletic.

Premium healthcare

Receive private health insurance giving you peace of mind for your health needs.

Extra days off

Enjoy additional vacation days off as you grow with us. Plus, get extra days for sick leave, special occasions, or parenting needs.

Joyful moments – special treats

Celebrate life’s big moments with special gifts from us on your birthday, anniversary, and other major events, such as weddings or the arrival of a new family member.

Company events & team-building

Experience iconic Nord Security celebrations, team-buildings, and knowledge-sharing events, nurturing bonds that fuel our success.

Workation

Embark on a legendary company getaway abroad, filled with exciting activities, live concerts, engaging workshops, and epic time together.

 

Kindly refer to our Privacy Notice for Recruitment Candidates https://drive.google.com/file/d/1b2tV684_SYV1jQ4kuf91cnzrRBk3ef-5/view for comprehensive information regarding our data handling procedures throughout recruitment processes.

We expect all candidates to provide accurate and complete information during the recruitment process. While limited use of AI tools to refine application materials is acceptable, candidates remain fully responsible for ensuring that their submissions reflect their own qualifications, skills, and experience. Any failure to do so may negatively affect participation in the recruitment process. If broader AI assistance is allowed for a particular role or stage, we’ll let you know in advance.

By submitting your application, you acknowledge that it may be processed using automated tools for evaluation purposes. As part of our recruitment process, we may use an AI-based application review tool to help assess applications based on skills and experience relevant to the role. This technology is used to support - not replace - human decision-making, and every application is ultimately reviewed by a recruiter.

If you would like more information about how AI is used in this process or wish to exercise your rights under applicable data privacy laws, please contact us at privacy@nordaccount.com. Should you prefer to opt out of the automated evaluation, please submit your application directly to career@nordsec.com.
